# CONSTELLA

# UI Architecture Specification

Version : 1.0

---

# 1. Purpose

This document defines the complete User Interface architecture of Constella.

The objective is to create a consistent, scalable and intuitive interface where users spend their time inside **Spaces** instead of navigating complex menus.

The UI should feel like a calm workspace rather than a productivity dashboard.

Every interaction should reduce friction while encouraging users to continuously build their Spaces.

---

# 2. Design Principles

The interface follows these principles.

• Minimal

• Fast

• Search First

• Keyboard Friendly

• Local First

• Context Aware

• Distraction Free

• Responsive

• Consistent

The interface should never overwhelm users with unnecessary controls.

Every action should require the minimum possible interaction.

---

# 3. Application Layout

Desktop Layout

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Top Navigation                                                              │
├──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────┤
│              │                                              │               │
│              │                                              │               │
│ Sidebar      │              Workspace                       │ Inspector     │
│              │                                              │               │
│              │                                              │               │
├──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────┤
│ Status Bar                                                                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Only five permanent UI regions exist.

Top Navigation

Sidebar

Workspace

Inspector

Status Bar

No floating permanent windows.

