# 36. Empty States

Every screen should provide helpful empty states.

Example

No Spaces

"Create your first Space."

No Artifacts

"Start capturing knowledge."

No Search Results

"No matching content found."

No Timeline

"Your journey will appear here."

No generic blank screens.

---

# 37. Loading States

Use skeleton loaders.

Avoid blocking the interface.

Search results should appear progressively.

Large media should lazy-load.

Background synchronization should never freeze the UI.

---

# 38. Notifications

Notification Types

Success

Warning

Error

Information

Events

Sync Complete

Sync Failed

Backup Created

Backup Restored

Conflict Detected

Storage Connected

AI Finished

Notifications disappear automatically except for errors requiring user action.

---

# 39. Accessibility

Minimum Requirements

Keyboard Navigation

Focus Indicators

Screen Reader Labels

High Contrast Support

Scalable Text

Accessible Color Contrast

The application should remain usable without a mouse.

---

# 40. Interaction Rules

Every interaction in Constella follows these rules.

1. Every change saves automatically.

2. The interface never blocks while synchronizing.

3. Every object is searchable.

4. Every Artifact opens in the same editor.

5. Every Space has the same navigation structure.

6. Every dialog can be closed using the keyboard.

7. Context menus remain consistent throughout the application.

8. Search is always one shortcut away.

9. The user should never manually organize files or folders.

10. Cloud availability must never affect normal editing.

---

# 41. Visual Design System

Design Style

Minimal

Professional

Modern

Calm

The application should emphasize content over decoration.

Use whitespace generously.

Avoid unnecessary gradients, glassmorphism or heavy animations.

Primary focus should always remain on the current Space and its knowledge.

---

